Project Title: Home Price Prediction Model
Project Description

The Home Price Prediction Model is a Machine Learning project that estimates the selling price of a house based on various features such as location, area, number of bedrooms, bathrooms, age of the property, and other relevant attributes. The goal is to help buyers, sellers, and real estate businesses make informed pricing decisions using data-driven predictions.

The project involves collecting and preprocessing housing data, performing exploratory data analysis (EDA), selecting important features, and training regression models to predict house prices accurately. Popular algorithms such as Linear Regression, Decision Tree Regressor, Random Forest Regressor, and XGBoost Regressor can be used and compared to identify the best-performing model.

Key Features
Predicts house prices based on user inputs.
Performs data cleaning and preprocessing.
Uses feature engineering for better accuracy.
Compares multiple machine learning regression algorithms.
Evaluates model performance using metrics like:
Mean Absolute Error (MAE)
Mean Squared Error (MSE)
Root Mean Squared Error (RMSE)
R² Score
Can be deployed as a web application using Flask or Streamlit.
Technologies Used
Python
Pandas
NumPy
Scikit-learn
Matplotlib & Seaborn
Jupyter Notebook
Flask/Streamlit (for deployment)
Applications
Real estate price estimation
Property valuation
Investment decision support
Housing market analysis

This project demonstrates the practical application of Machine Learning Regression techniques to solve real-world real estate pricing problems by providing fast and accurate house price predictions.
